<h2>The purpose test</h2>

<p>The starting point is functional. Custody pending trial serves three interests: presence at trial, integrity of evidence, and prevention of further offences. Bail substitutes conditions for custody in service of the same three interests. A condition that serves none of them is not a bail condition at all — it is an exaction. That single test resolves most disputes about conditions, and it is the test Delhi courts apply when modification is sought.</p>

<table class="law">
  <tr><th>Condition</th><th>Purpose served</th><th>Standing</th></tr>
